// WebGLEngine/brain/subCountermeasures-selfcheck.mjs -- UNNUMBERED (the version is chosen at ship time)
//
// Run: node brain/subCountermeasures-selfcheck.mjs      (about 20 s: fixtures, a few torpedo steps, a handful of duels and fights of DEV seeds 1 to 4 -- NEVER a registered seed)
//
// THE GATE OF brain/subCountermeasures.mjs, OF THE THREE ADDITIVE OPTIONS IN physics/mechanics/subTorpedo.mjs (`sl`, `screens`, `params`), OF THE HOOKS IN brain/subDuel.mjs AND brain/seaOgre.mjs, AND OF tools/ship/takeCountermeasures.mjs
// (the registration is brain/SUB_COUNTERMEASURES_WIP.md, with Amendments A and B):
//   1 CONSTANTS     the chosen numbers to the digit (they are choices, said), the kits, the id ranges
//   2 SCREENLOSS    the line-through-a-sphere test: through, tangent, just outside, beyond the end, ending inside, two screens (the larger), three dimensions, a zero-length line
//   3 THE TORPEDO   `sl` (the louder decoy wins the cone; a quieter one does not; an absent or non-finite one is the old rule), `screens` (a boat behind one is not locked; one off the line is), `params` (the cruise and the launch speed), and nothing changed when none is given
//   4 THE ENGINE    createCm: what an order releases and when (inventory, spacing in whole ticks, sides alternating), the decoys' drift and life, the screens' life, the interceptor's launch and clamps, stepInterceptors (a kill, a friend spared, a refusal to hunt) and the counts
//   5 THE WRAPPER   withCountermeasures: the thresholds, the louder torpedo, the absolute bearing, the rate limits, the enabled flags, the wrapped order untouched
//   6 THE ARENAS    with no kit the duel and the fight are the ORIGINAL code's, to the fingerprint (pins taken from the files before the hooks); with a kit the numbers of DEV geometry 1 and OGRE scenario 4; the events and the result's `cm`
//   7 THE COMMAND   arguments and refusals, the reading rule at its edges, sideOf, duelMatchup, a DEV flow on one seed, a stubbed HELD75 flow and its rows, the command run as a program
//   8 THE SOURCE    no clock, no random number; the imports; the headers; the registration
// NOT CHECKED, said plainly: that any of this is a good design of a countermeasure (the numbers are chosen, not measured), and which kit wins the registered read (that is the experiment).
//
// SABOTAGES (2026-11-07; the harness mutates a COPY of the target in an isolated tree whose directories are real, never the real file -- the pass of 2026-11-06 was made through a symlink and left a mutant in subTorpedo.mjs, so it was thrown away and everything below is a redo; sha256 of the six files
// checked before and after every chain and identical; `git status` shows no stray file):
//   PASS 1, the gate as first written (69 rows). Mechanical mutants (an operator, a comparison, a number plus or minus one, a boolean, a negation, one at a time, each line of the target) and hand mutants (a named behaviour broken), each run against this gate:
//     brain/subCountermeasures.mjs   233 line mutants + 229 token mutants + 35 hand: all but 36 red by name or by a crash (16 of the red were crashes of the gate), 33 + 3 left alive
//     physics/mechanics/subTorpedo.mjs   130 mechanical + 12 hand: 15 left alive         brain/subDuel.mjs (the hook)   14 + 8: 3 alive         brain/seaOgre.mjs (the hook)   12 + 10: 4 alive
//     tools/ship/takeCountermeasures.mjs   171 line mutants + 171 token mutants + 15 hand: 40 alive
//     The 22 that were left alive in the torpedo, the duel hook and the OGRE hook were also run against those modules' own gates: 6 died there (torpedo); 16 stood and are below.
//   WHAT THE SURVIVORS SHOWED (each is a row now): the launch id and the whole fresh state of a torpedo; the defaults of stepTorpedo and of stepInterceptors (dt, tick, seed -- found by a search for geometries where the sonar luck moves the kill by a tick); a screen on a segment shorter than a metre;
//     carries() with ONE of a mechanism; the edges of isDecoy; the elevation of an interceptor (none is 0, 0.6 and 1.0 and 2.0 clamp to one kill tick, -2 and -0.6 to another -- seen through the kill tick of a torpedo coming along the bearing); a release copies the position (a live
//     array would move the decoy and the screen with the boat); a tie in SNR keeps the first torpedo; the wrapper's defaults; the report lines to the character; a kit in SEAT A (the swapped geometry 2: the DEV geometries never shoot at seat A, so the inventory of boat 1 was never used);
//     a kit on both sides; the OGRE fight with the DECOY kit alone (the only DEV case with a decoyed event: its tick, its `boat: 0`, no hit after it -- without the row the missing `continue` was a crash nobody had ever seen); the command's output on two geometries and on the four OGRE
//     scenarios to the character, and the stubbed HELD75 file to the byte (sha256); the command run as a program with NO argument (the guard read the first ARGUMENT, not the program name); and the checks that make a read void: they were inline, unreachable in a test, so they are
//     now duelChecks and ogreChecks (exported, tested one condition at a time) and `command` takes `io.checks` to show the NOT WEIGHED line in the output -- the one change to a module made for the gate, and every line it touched was re-mutated (PASS 3).
//   PASS 2, the gate with its 88 rows: the 92 survivors of pass 1 re-run: 68 red, 1 crash (the OGRE hook without the `continue` after a decoyed event -- the fight throws), 23 alive. EQUIVALENT, argued, not killed:
//     subCountermeasures.mjs  the clamp's `>` and `<` made `>=` and `<=` (the bound is returned either way); four numbers and operators inside the JSDoc (the generator does not skip a ` * ` line); the decoy's vertical velocity 0 -> 1 (nothing reads it: the position
//       steps by x and y only); the 180 of the report's degrees -> 179 and 181 (50.28 and 49.72 both print as 50 with toFixed(0))
//     subTorpedo.mjs  a number in the JSDoc; the `: 0` of a zero-length segment (dx, dy and dz are all 0 there, so u multiplies nothing); `sc.db > loss` -> `>=` (it assigns an equal value)
//     seaOgre.mjs  "a defender's own torpedoes can be decoyed" (the isDecoy test without `theirs`): the defenders' torpedoes aim at the OGRE's zones (901 to 904) and escorts (800 to 899), none inside the decoy range 2000 to 2999, so the test is false for them either way
//     takeCountermeasures.mjs  the side labels "d" + i and "all@" + thr (a label nothing prints) -- the other eight died when the checks were made testable (PASS 3)
//   PASS 3, the command after the refactor: the 20 mutants of the lines it changed (16 red, 4 crashes) and the 15 hand mutants again (14 red, 1 crash): none alive. The mutants of the lines it did not touch were killed in passes 1 and 2 by rows that were only added to, never relaxed
//     (the one row replaced, a regular expression over the source for the NOT WEIGHED text, is replaced by a run that shows the line).
// NOT SABOTAGED: the gate's own section 8 (the headers and the registration are read as text), and the numbers of the registered read (they are not code).
